{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And he did not know anything about him except the bread.</b> Some say it is a euphemism for lying with his wife. This is far-fetched, and moreover, because Joseph's master was a eunuch. The correct view in my eyes is that everything he had was in his hand except the bread, which he did not even touch, because he was a Hebrew, for it is explicitly stated: \"for the Egyptians could not eat bread with the Hebrews\" (Genesis 43:32), since Potiphar knew that Joseph was a Hebrew, and likewise his wife says: \"See, he brought us a Hebrew man\" (Genesis 39:14)." "<b>And Joseph was beautiful of form.</b> Like his mother."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:47:28.294793093Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}